.TH VC4TRAIN 1 "2026-11-20" "vc4-stack" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vc4train \- toy QPU trainer (MLP 64-32-10) for the VideoCore IV engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vc4train
[\fB\-\-opt\fR \fIsgd\fR|\fIadam\fR] [\fB\-\-steps\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trains a two-layer MLP full batch on a fixed synthetic 10-class dataset.
Every multiply-accumulate, activation, the fused softmax + cross-entropy
gradient and the optimizer step run as QPU kernels; the ARM only prepares
buffers and prints the loss.
.PP
The program exits non-zero unless the training loss drops at least 5x and the
test accuracy reaches 90%.  It is a check that the installed engine has working
backward kernels, not a training framework.
.PP
With
.B VC4INFER_DAEMON=1
(set by
.IR /etc/profile.d/vc4.sh )
launches go through
.IR /run/vc4d.sock
unprivileged; otherwise the binary needs root and
.IR /dev/mem .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-opt \fIsgd\fR|\fIadam\fR
Optimizer (default sgd).
.TP
.B \-\-steps \fIN\fR
Number of optimizer steps (default 300).
.TP
.B \-\-seed \fIS\fR
PRNG seed (default 12345).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vc4-query (1),
.BR vc4infer (1)
